WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.466 --> 00:00:02.572
(child cries)
(tense music)

00:00:02.572 --> 00:00:03.510
(bomb explodes)
(child cries)

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.303
- [Narrator] After a brief
period of upheaval in Russia,

00:00:06.303 --> 00:00:07.530
(crowd cheer)

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.660
in which President Vladimir Putin's regime

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.120
was tested, perhaps, more than at any time

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.354
in its over 20 years in power,

00:00:14.354 --> 00:00:15.187
(gun shots)

00:00:15.187 --> 00:00:18.381
focus has returned to the front
lines of the war in Ukraine.

00:00:18.381 --> 00:00:19.214
(gun fires)

00:00:19.214 --> 00:00:21.060
- I'd say the counter-offensive
has been going slowly.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.910
Ukraine's allies certainly hoped

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.240
for more progress by this
point than we've seen.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.830
- I can't emphasize
enough how difficult it is

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.720
for a unit to get through
this obstacle belt from hell.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.110
It's among the toughest
military operations

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.540
that anybody can anticipate.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.970
- [Narrator] Here's the situation
on the ground right now,

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:48.607
and what to expect next
on the battlefield.

00:00:48.607 --> 00:00:50.520
(gun fires)
(bomb explodes)

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.720
In early June,

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.565
Ukraine began its long
awaited counter-offensive

00:00:54.565 --> 00:00:55.530
(gun shots)

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.270
with much of the fighting concentrated

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.600
in the southern regions of
Zaporizhzhia and Donetsk.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.950
- In those first days,

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:06.950
there were big armed
formations pushing forward.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.996
They were using German leopard tanks,

00:01:11.996 --> 00:01:12.829
(man speaks foreign language)

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:15.660
they were using American
Bradley fighting vehicles.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.970
The terrain in the Zaporizhzhia region

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.240
where they're trying to push
forward is very unforgiving

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.380
for an attacking force.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.460
It's very agricultural,

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.550
it's mostly very flat open
fields you can see for miles.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.204
So there's very little cover.

00:01:28.204 --> 00:01:32.537
- (Yevgeny speaks foreign language)

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.260
- [Narrator] Then on Friday, June 23rd,

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.710
tensions between the Russian
paramilitary organization known

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.710
as the Wagner Group, and
Russian military leaders

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.310
boiled over after Wagner
leader Yevgeny Prigozhin said,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.650
the Russian military
had killed a huge number

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.873
of his troops in an airstrike.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:56.100
But as quickly as the revolt
had started, it fizzled.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.340
Less than 24 hours after
the mutiny was launched,

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.520
the two sides reached what
appeared to be a truce.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.910
- I don't think the mutiny
has had a significant effect

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.440
of any kind on the counter offensive.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.659
The Ukrainians were in
this holding pattern

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:11.940
(gun shots)

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.220
where they're probing for weak spots

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.410
and that's what they were
doing before the mutiny

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.903
and that's still what they're doing.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.353
- So the situation on the
ground right now, candidly,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.520
there hasn't been a
significant amount of progress.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.390
- [Narrator] Mark Kimmitt

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.910
is retired US Army Brigadier General

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:33.690
who served in Bosnia, Kosovo, and Iraq.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:37.170
- There are three attacks,
significant attacks going on

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.590
as the Ukrainians are trying to figure out

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.713
the soft spots along the front.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.520
The first, this is down here by Bakhmut.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.900
It is flipped back and forth

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.230
between the Ukrainian and
Russian forces numerous times.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.140
If the Ukrainians were
able to blow through there,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.450
I think that they would go further down

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.260
to the Southeast as far
as possible to the border.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.630
The second area where they
seem to be putting a lot

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.300
of pressure on is down
here by Zaporizhzhia.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.950
Obviously, not only is the
nuclear plant significant,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.620
but this also gives a breakthrough route

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.170
that takes you all the way to Berdyansk.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.690
If this Ukrainian force was able

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:22.710
to break through to Berdyansk,
there would be a cutting off

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:26.370
of the land bridge up towards the Donetsk.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.130
There's a lot of fighting going up here

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.020
near Vuhledar as well.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:35.730
Same idea, this would give
them a route through Donetsk,

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:39.213
down to Mariupol, or could
take it straight to Mariupol.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.020
- [Narrator] On June 6th,
the Nova Kakhovka Dam

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.090
on the Dnipro River was breached,

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:48.480
releasing a flood of water from
Ukraine's largest reservoir.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.730
- The Russians, fearing that this was

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:55.410
the number one attack
route to split off Crimea

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:58.110
and also get out to the water,

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.830
they flooded the dam down
here at Nova Kakhovka.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.660
Well, it's starting to dry out again

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.960
and the water is going into the Black Sea.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.850
That gives the potential for
the Ukrainian forces here

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.850
in Kherson to start the attack.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:15.960
- [Narrator] The slow progress

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.420
of the Ukrainian counter-offensive,
especially in the wake

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:21.330
of the recent chaos in
Russia, raises questions.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.896
Why is the counter-offensive
taking so long

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.870
(gun shots)

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.960
and why have the Ukrainians
had such limited success

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.240
breaking through the front lines?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.520
- [Mark] This is 20 kilometers of hell.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.510
There's absolutely no
doubt that it is probably

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:39.720
the toughest fighting
outside of the cities

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.250
- [Narrator] According to General Kimmitt,

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.080
part of the reason why
the counter-offensive

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.480
has been so challenging
is that the frontline

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.940
is about 600 miles long.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.040
What's more, the Russians have had months

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.510
to prepare their defenses,

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.390
which are made up of a
series of layered obstacles.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.400
- What the Ukrainians are trying to do

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.250
is find the soft spot in that defense.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.400
Now, this is just not
a couple of barriers,

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.920
the Russians, like most countries,

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.770
have what they call a deliberate defense

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:10.950
which is a series of layered obstacles,

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.610
all to make sure that the Ukrainian forces

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:18.450
are stopped as far forward as possible.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:22.650
So you have an overscale
Ukrainian vehicle here.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:27.650
That mechanized company is
first going to hit a tank trap.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.760
What a tank trap is,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:34.050
the whole idea is to have
the vehicle go into the trap

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:37.530
and then come up and to
get over and out of that,

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.803
he's going to expose his
underbelly right here.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.310
The fact is that the softest spot

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.980
on this vehicle is not the
front, it's not the side,

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.740
it's not the top, but it's the underbelly.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.590
And as it shows its belly,

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.470
it can be engaged by direct fire weapons.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:58.110
So the next obstacle
will be for the troops.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.490
It will be this layer

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.360
of barbed wire that the
troops will be caught up in.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.060
And here from the trench lines,

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:11.060
you have soldiers firing
anti-tank weapons, machine guns

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.190
and then what's left of that force,

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:16.920
will try to get in and
through the trench line

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.730
with both dismounted soldiers
and mounted soldiers.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.830
The vehicles and the troops now

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.230
have to cross these trench lines.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.690
No doubt, there's a lot
of hand-to-hand fighting

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.690
because if the vehicles
start coming across

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:34.840
in these trench lines can now
fire from the side, mayhem.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.310
Absolute mayhem on both sides.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:41.340
Those that do get through
and there will be very few,

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:44.160
it would probably have
to be a follow on unit

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.450
that does it through this
punched hole that they have,

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:53.450
will then hit the mines, these
little dots or minefields.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.830
Should they make it through there,

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.900
then they hit the dragon teeth.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:02.900
These are very, very
sturdy concrete triangles.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:07.080
They will stop a vehicle if
he tries to drive through it.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.150
And again, to get over it,

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:12.240
he has to expose his belly to get over it.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.160
If this unit gets through,

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:19.160
then they will be hit by
casemated, fixed bunkers,

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.320
much like you saw in
"Saving Private Ryan."

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.480
The Russians will be firing artillery,

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.880
they'll be firing cluster munitions,

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:31.413
they'll be attacked by
aircraft, helicopters, drones.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.880
And so you, it is not
difficult to understand

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.390
why it's so hard to break through.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.880
- [Narrator] Despite limited
gains on the front lines,

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.730
the Russian Revolt has
provided Ukrainian troops

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.230
with a morale boost.

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.600
- One thing that I have heard repeatedly

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.270
from Ukrainian troops, especially
the ones who were fighting

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.120
in the East, was that it
was much tougher coming up

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.460
against Wagner than it was coming up

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.800
against regular Russian
troops for the most part,

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.000
that they were more experienced,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.310
that they were better trained,
that they were braver.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.860
But again, they were no
longer on the front lines,

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.930
and they had been an
assaulting force all through

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:07.770
the war up to this point.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:10.110
And right now, Russia's
in a defensive posture

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.380
and that's frankly, that's
the easier task, is defending.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.870
- That morale boost needs to be seen

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.510
by tangible progress on the ground.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:23.220
And candidly, we're not seeing
it since the mutiny started.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.053
- Welcome.

00:08:24.053 --> 00:08:26.820
- [Narrator] In a July 6th
interview with ABC News,

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.520
President Zelenskyy said
the counter-offensive

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.094
was going to plan.

00:08:31.094 --> 00:08:32.730
- (Zelenskyy speaks foreign language)

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:34.710
- [Translator] We all
want to do it faster.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:38.507
The president told me,
every day means new losses.

00:08:38.507 --> 00:08:39.990
(engine revs)

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.180
- [Narrator] To help
push back Russian forces,

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:44.880
on July 7th, the Biden administration said

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.000
it would be providing
cluster munitions to Ukraine.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.160
- We will not leave Ukraine defenseless

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.290
at any point in this conflict period.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.240
- I think the thing to watch is,

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.810
at some point we're going
to see large formations

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.700
with dozens of Western tanks.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.170
We haven't seen that.

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.720
And I think that that will be when

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:06.564
the counter-offensive
is really in full swing.

00:09:06.564 --> 00:09:08.565
(soldier speaks foreign language)

00:09:08.565 --> 00:09:10.021
(gun shots)

00:09:10.021 --> 00:09:11.722
(soldier speaks foreign language)

00:09:11.722 --> 00:09:12.711
(bright music)

